    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d55">

                <pb facs="0177" n="83" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg83"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Jones to Mr.
                            Rockhill.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Chinkiang</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-11-24"><hi rendition="#italic">November 24, 1896</hi></date>.
                        (Received Dec. 22.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 282.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    by mail on the 18th instant of Department instructions No. 91, dated October 12,
                    1896, sent direct, in which I am informed that it is expected that I will see
                    that the magistrate at Kiangyin is dismissed promptly from office, as promised,
                    and that a proclamation is posted throughout Kiangyin stating the ground of his
                    dismissal.</p>
                <p>The Department can be assured that this will receive my earnest attention in all
                    particulars in compliance with instructions.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. C. Jones</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Consul</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
